lowers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-15T22:59:33Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T22:59:33Z","body":"Yeah, very likely caused by that, we need to come up with a nice way to support both iterations because one is correct in mono rendering, the other is correct for stereo rendering... Sigh.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3757292272/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3758048378","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114995#issuecomment-3758048378","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114995","id":3758048378,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7f_0R6","user":{"login":"Clubhouse1661","id":177586398,"node_id":"U_kgDOCpXA3g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177586398?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clubhouse1661","html_url":"https://github.com/Clubhouse1661","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clubhouse1661/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clubhouse1661/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clubhouse1661/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clubhouse1661/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clubhouse1661/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clubhouse1661/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clubhouse1661/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clubhouse1661/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clubhouse1661/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-16T04:10:50Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T04:10:50Z","body":"I've created a fix for this issue that addresses @BastiaanOlij's concern about supporting both mono and stereo rendering correctly.\n\nThe solution uses `EYE_OFFSET` to detect the rendering mode at runtime:\n- **Mono rendering**: `EYE_OFFSET == vec3(0,0,0)` → uses `abs((MODELVIEW_MATRIX)[3].z)` \n- **Stereo/XR rendering**: `EYE_OFFSET` is non-zero → uses `length((MODELVIEW_MATRIX)[3].xyz)` \n\nThis preserves the fix from #110410 for XR while restoring correct behavior in mono mode.\n\nPR: #115020\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3758048378/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]